    "customer_concern": "front bumper paint krna hai, fender py dry dent hai woh thk krwana hai, suspension sy awazain a rhi hain, gari ki tuning b hony wali hai, oil change b hony wala hai, gari left side ki trf b khinchti hai",
    "ai_diagnosis_result": {
      "roman_urdu_explanation": "1. Front Bumper Paint aur Fender Dry Denting: Aap ki gari ke aglay bumper par scratches hain aur fender par dry dent hai. Bumper ko proper sanding, primer aur 2K paint match kar ke original showroom shine di jaye gi, jabke fender ka dent bina paint kharab kiye dry denting tool se nikaala jaye ga. 2. Suspension Awazain aur Left Side Pulling: Front suspension ke lower arm bushes aur tie rod ends ghiss chuke hain jis ki wajah se gadday par awazain aati hain aur gari left side par pull karti hai. Agar isay theek na karwaya jaye tu mehngay tyres ek taraf se ghalat ghis jayen ge (uneven tyre wear) aur steering control kamzor ho jaye ga. Al Shaheen Auto Hub par suspension overhauling ke baad computerized 3D wheel alignment aur balancing ki jaye gi. 3. Engine Tuning aur Engine Oil Change: 45,000 KM par gari ki routine maintenance required hai. Throttle body, spark plugs aur air filter ki safai/replacement ke sath Toyota OEM engine oil aur oil filter change kiya jaye ga taake fuel average aur pick behtar ho sakay.",
      "plain_english_explanation": "The vehicle requires cosmetic body repairs, routine engine servicing, and suspension overhauling. The front bumper has paint scuffs requiring a complete professional repainting, while the front fender features a minor dent suitable for Paintless Dent Repair (PDR). The noise from the undercarriage and vehicle pulling towards the left side stems from worn front lower arm bushings, tie rod ends, and wheel misalignment. Post-suspension repair, a 3D computerized alignment and wheel balancing will resolve the tracking issue. Additionally, a full engine tune-up (throttle body cleaning, spark plug service, air filter replacement) and an oil service at 45,000 KM will restore optimal engine performance and efficiency.",
      "mechanical_root_cause": "1. Suspension Noise & Left Pulling: Deteriorated front lower control arm rubber bushings and worn tie rod end joints causing excessive play in the front suspension geometry, resulting in dynamic camber/caster deviation and vehicle pulling to the left under load. 2. Engine Hesitation / Service Due: Carbon buildup on the electronic throttle body butterfly valve and degraded spark plug electrode gap at 45,000 KM causing sluggish acceleration. 3. Cosmetic Body Damage: Surface paint abrasion on front bumper fascia and localized sheet metal deformation on fender without paint fracture.",
      "recommended_departments": [
        "Mechanical",
        "Suspension",
        "Alignment",
        "Balancing",
        "Denting",
        "Painting",
        "General Service"
      ],
      "work_to_be_done": "1. Disassemble front bumper fascia, perform surface preparation, primer application, computer color matching, and 2K clear coat paint booth baking. 2. Perform Paintless Dent Repair (PDR / Dry Denting) on the damaged front fender using specialized PDR rods and suction tools. 3. Inspect front suspension linkage; replace worn lower control arm bushes and outer tie rod ends. 4. Drain engine oil, replace Toyota genuine oil filter, and refill with 3.7L 5W-30 synthetic engine oil. 5. Perform complete engine tuning: remove and clean electronic throttle body with cleaner spray, inspect/clean/replace spark plugs, clean intake air filter, and reset ECU self-learned parameters. 6. Execute 4-wheel computerized 3D alignment and dynamic wheel balancing to eliminate left-side drift.",
